  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Financing Solutions for the Decarbonization of Viet Nam#s Cement Industry</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This item is a replica of the project SAP ID. 250072 and was created for the purpose of receiving external PA funding.  Description: The project, led by UNIDO with support from Guidehouse Germany GmBH. International Finance Corporation, French Agency for Development, and local institutions in Viet Nam, aims to catalyze a transformational shift in Vietnam#s cement industry by implementing cement decarbonization projects and establishing the conditions necessary for broader market uptake of low-carbon technologies in the cement sector. It intends to directly address five interconnected barriers including financial, technical, structural, regulatory, and behavioral through an integrated approach combining investment, technical assistance, and policy reform. Central to the intervention is a tailored financial mechanism, jointly designed and implemented with local and international financial partners, that de-risks private investments and facilitates access to concessional capital. This includes concessional loans, sustainability-linked loans and potentially credit line from local financial institution with embedded grant and technical support to incentivize the uptake of mitigation technologies like LC3 adoptions, SCM optimization, WHR installation.</narrative>
  </description>
